  "methodology": "Census tract estimates apportioned to City Council districts by area-weighted overlay: each tract's counts are split across districts in proportion to the share of the tract's land area falling in each district, then summed per district. District boundaries: seattleio/seattle-boundaries-data (community-maintained, not an official City of Seattle GIS source). Tract boundaries: US Census Bureau TIGER/Line cartographic boundary files, 2023 vintage. Citywide figures are queried directly at the Seattle place level, not resummed from districts. ACS 5-year estimates carry sampling error that can be substantial at the tract level; treat percentages as estimates, not precise counts.",
